    "explanation": "Both parties' arithmetic, and the record, agree on the governing measurement. The GPS trace EV-GPS-00102 (weight 1.0) records trace_distance_km 21.79 against the booked optimal of 20.4 km on EV-TRIP-00102, an excess of 1.39 km — 6.81% of optimal. POL-RD-01 establishes a route deviation only when the excess is greater than 20% of optimal AND greater than 0.8 km absolute, and both limbs must pass. The absolute limb is met (1.39 km > 0.8 km) but the percentage limb is not (6.81% against 20%, i.e. 4.08 km for this optimal). No deviation is established, and POL-RD-01 fixes the outcome at NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip. The trace figure governs, not the rounded 21.8 km convenience copy on the trip record, but either figure gives the same result. The trace is unimpaired: 100% coverage, 193 fixes, no gaps, 10 s sampling, so POL-RD-07 and POL-RD-10(3) are not engaged.\n\nOn the rider's points: (1) The driver's chat message EV-CHAT-00102 — 'boss BKE quite jam, i go Upper Bukit Timah ok?' at 11:29:04, read 11:29:40 — is accepted as showing the vehicle left the BKE corridor, and the driver's counterparty statement accepts the same. But POL-RD-01's establishment test is numeric, and an admitted corridor change does not substitute for an excess clearing 20%; the same evidence confirms the change was small ('same distance more or less'; 1.39 km on the trace). (2) The fare differential is accepted as arithmetic but is not payable: charged_total 29.91 less the platform's recomputed optimal fare 27.46 is 2.45, but POL-RD-02 runs only on a deviation first established under POL-RD-01, and none is. The 29.91 is the metered fare correctly built from base 3.80 + distance 16.35 + time 8.96 + platform fee 0.80 for the distance and time actually driven. (3) POL-RD-09(4) gives nothing: erp_gantries is empty, tolls_erp 0.00 and airport_surcharge 0.00, so there is no phantom gantry line or misapplied surcharge to correct, and that is the only route to money on a no-deviation finding.\n\nOn the driver's points: the assertion of a BKE crawl near Dairy Farm is an external-traffic assertion. The only traffic advisory for this trip, EV-ADVIS-00102-01, is MISSING — status MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — and no LTA advisory covers the BKE or the Upper Bukit Timah corridor in the 11:16–11:55 window. Under POL-RD-13 and POL-RD-08 the comparison cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and the assertion carries no weight; it neither reduces the excess nor supplies an amended optimal. The driver cites no advisory identifier for the excuse, so the absence is a gap in the bundle and not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation. The point is in any event immaterial: with no deviation established there is nothing to exculpate.\n\nPOL-RD-04 is unavailable: the corridor instruction came from the DRIVER, not the rider, the rider never replied, and chat_message.waypoint_hint is null, so there is no rider-requested detour to corroborate. POL-RD-06 is not engaged — no material deviation, and driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 of 640 completed trips — so no conduct referral fires. POL-RD-11 does not apply (fare_model METERED, not UPFRONT_QUOTE) and POL-RD-12 does not apply (vehicle_type RYDE_PLUS, not RYDE_POOL). No billing-integrity referral under POL-RD-09(4) and no false-arrival referral arise.\n\nConfidence: the deciding fact — the excess measurement — is carried by EV-GPS-00102 and EV-TRIP-00102, both at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0. The MISSING advisory at weight 0.0 carries no fact and does not cap anything. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: identifiers all match TRP-00102, timestamps agree, no cited artifact is missing in support of an invoked exculpatory clause, and no refund exceeds the ceiling.\n\nOutcome: the rider's claim is not supported on this record. payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00 stand as they are; the disputed 29.91 is neither refunded nor held, and no money moves to either party.",
